From 73167b6757ad31d595c41b38db1e166b3afd0061 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 04:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][3D] An HDR 3D video goes out as SDR by default: 3D
 displays take no HDR in 3D

"How 3D video goes out" (videoscreen.hades3dcolour) sent an HDR 3D
video as HDR on Automatic wherever the display takes HDR. A projector
that takes HDR10 then refused its 3D mode ("3D settings are not
supported in HDR video", a Dolby Vision 3D film rebuilt as HDR10, side
by side at 3840x2160), and its owner had to find the setting and choose
SDR in BT.2020. 3D TVs and projectors take no HDR in 3D, and nothing
they send says so beforehand: an EDID declares HDR for 2D only.

Automatic is now SDR in 3D, in the gamut of "HDR to SDR: gamut of the
output", which every 3D display shows, as 3D Blu-ray discs are: an HDR
3D video, a Dolby Vision 3D film rebuilt, is mapped to SDR as on a
display without HDR. HDR is still there to choose, for a display that
takes HDR in 3D, and SDR in BT.2020 or BT.709 as before. 2D videos and
SDR 3D videos do not change; the user's own choice for a video ("As
SDR") still comes first. kodi.log names the choice and what it sends,
and the help of the setting says it in plain words (English and the
three Spanish translations of Estuary).
