-msgid "For those who try what their 3D TV or projector takes. Automatic: an HDR 3D video goes out as HDR where the display takes its HDR, and as SDR elsewhere, in the gamut of \"HDR to SDR: gamut of the output\", as without this setting. HDR: HDR10 (an HLG video in HLG, Dolby Vision rebuilt as HDR10), also where \"Play HDR videos as SDR\" says otherwise. SDR in BT.2020 or SDR in BT.709: every HDR 3D video mapped to SDR in that gamut, as in 2D, also on a display that takes HDR. What is chosen goes out only where the display says in its EDID that it takes it and the graphics driver can send it; elsewhere what Automatic sends, and the player information and kodi.log say so. A Dolby Vision 3D film (profile 20) is rebuilt in 3D whatever is chosen. SDR 3D videos go out as they are. Applies from the next video."
